Priority Queue:
=============
    a) A data structure where elements are retrieved based upon priority. (Heaps are used to implement Priority Queue)
    b) There are group of elements stored, return the one which has highest priority.

                                   PriorityQueue
                                  /             \
                                 /               \
                                /                 \
                    min PriorityQueue       max PriorityQueue
                      (min heap)                (max heap)
                   [increasing order]      [decreasing order]

    • The default implementation of PriorityQueue uses a Min-Heap (smallest element at the top).
    • Max-Heap can be implemented by providing a custom comparator.

==============================================================================================
******.  PriorityQueue is implemented as a min-heap by default. (for natural ordering) *****
==============================================================================================

1. Priority can be element itself or a property related to the element
   For e.g..,
      a)  Given 10 numbers, find the smallest & 2nd smallest element
          ==========================================================
      b)  Insert 5 more numbers, now return the smallest.

2. Property of element is priority
      a)  In a class, there are 20 students return the name of the student who got the
          highest marks.
          =============================================================================
      b)  If there are multiple  toppers, return the one whose name is lexicographically
          smaller.

3. Time Complexity of Priority Queue is O(log N)..   Since, it is based on Heap concepts.
